// Title: Potential Secure Deletion with SDelete
// Sigma ID: 39a80702-d7ca-4a83-b776-525b1f86a36d
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Thomas Patzke
// Date: 2017-06-14 | Modified: 2024-12-13
// ATT&CK: impact, stealth, defense-impairment, T1070.004, T1027.005, T1485, T1553.002, S0195
// Description: Detects files that have extensions commonly seen while SDelete is used to wipe files.
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate usage of SDelete
//   - Files that are interacted with that have these extensions legitimately
// References:
//   - https://jpcertcc.github.io/ToolAnalysisResultSheet/details/sdelete.htm
//   - https://www.jpcert.or.jp/english/pub/sr/ir_research.html
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-gb/sysinternals/downloads/sdelete
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/builtin/security/win_security_sdelete_potential_secure_deletion.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith ".AAA" or RegistryKey endswith ".ZZZ"
